94139539448 17592186576411 true] [17592186526070 1071 "$$\n\nIf $y=\\operatorname{arcoth}⁡{x}^{3}-\\frac{3}{4}{x}^{4},$ then $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=$" 13194139539448 17592186576411 false] [17592186526070 1071 "If $y=\\operatorname{arcoth}⁡{x}^{3}-\\frac{3}{4}{x}^{4},$ then $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=$" 13194139539448 17592186576411 true] [17592186526073 1071 "$$\n\nIf $y=\\operatorname{arcoth}⁡({x}^{2}-1),$ calculate $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}.$\n\n$\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=$\n{{field-1}}" 13194139539448 17592186576411 false] [17592186526073 1071 "If $y=\\operatorname{arcoth}⁡({x}^{2}-1),$ calculate $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}.$\n\n$\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=$\n{{field-1}}" 13194139539448 17592186576411 true] [17592186526079 1071 "$$\n\n$\\int (2{x}^{7}-\\frac{1}{8|x|\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+1}})\\text{d}x=$" 13194139539448 17592186576411 false] [17592186526079 1071 "$$\n\\int (2{x}^{7}-\\frac{1}{8|x|\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+1}})\\text{d}x=\n$$" 13194139539448 17592186576411 true] [17592186526079 1074 "$$\n\nThe formula for the derivative of the inverse hyperbolic cosecant function is\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\operatorname{arcsch}⁡x)=-\\frac{1}{|x|\\sqrt{1+{x}^{2}}}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int (2{x}^{7}-\\frac{1}{8|x|\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+1}})\\text{d}x & =\\int 2{x}^{7}\\,\\text{d}x-\\int \\frac{1}{8|x|\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+1}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =2\\int {x}^{7}\\,\\text{d}x+\\frac{1}{8}\\int -\\frac{1}{|x|\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+1}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}{x}^{8}+\\frac{1}{8}\\operatorname{arcsch}⁡x+C \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}({x}^{8}+\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{arcsch}⁡x)+C\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139539448 17592186576411 false] [17592186526079 1074 "The formula for the derivative of the inverse hyperbolic cosecant function is\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\operatorname{arcsch}⁡x)=-\\frac{1}{|x|\\sqrt{1+{x}^{2}}}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int (2{x}^{7}-\\frac{1}{8|x|\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+1}})\\text{d}x & =\\int 2{x}^{7}\\,\\text{d}x-\\int \\frac{1}{8|x|\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+1}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =2\\int {x}^{7}\\,\\text{d}x+\\frac{1}{8}\\int -\\frac{1}{|x|\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+1}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}{x}^{8}+\\frac{1}{8}\\operatorname{arcsch}⁡x+C \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}({x}^{8}+\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{arcsch}⁡x)+C\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139539448 17592186576411 true] [17592186526081 1071 "$$\n\n$\\int -\\frac{\\sqrt{e+1}}{|x|\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+1}}\\,\\text{d}x=$" 13194139539448 17592186576411 false] [17592186526081 1071 "$$\n\\int -\\frac{\\sqrt{e+1}}{|x|\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+1}}\\,\\text{d}x=\n$$" 13194139539448 17592186576411 true] [17592186526081 1074 "$$\n\nThe formula for the derivative of the inverse hyperbolic cosecant function is\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\operatorname{arcsch}⁡x)=-\\frac{1}{|x|\\sqrt{1+{x}^{2}}}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int -\\frac{\\sqrt{e+1}}{|x|\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+1}}\\,\\text{d}x=\\sqrt{e+1}\\int -\\frac{1}{|x|\\sqrt{1+{x}^{2}}}\\,\\text{d}x=\\sqrt{e+1}\\operatorname{arcsch}⁡x+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139539448 17592186576411 false] [17592186526081 1074 "The formula for the derivative of the inverse hyperbolic cosecant function is\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\operatorname{arcsch}⁡x)=-\\frac{1}{|x|\\sqrt{1+{x}^{2}}}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int -\\frac{\\sqrt{e+1}}{|x|\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+1}}\\,\\text{d}x=\\sqrt{e+1}\\int -\\frac{1}{|x|\\sqrt{1+{x}^{2}}}\\,\\text{d}x=\\sqrt{e+1}\\operatorname{arcsch}⁡x+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139539448 17592186576411 true] [17592186526090 1071 "$$\n\nIf $y=\\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}^{2}-1)+\\operatorname{arsech}⁡({x}^{2}-1),$ calculate $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}.$\n\n$\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{2x}{{x}^{2}-1}[1-$\n{{field-1}} $]$" 13194139539448 17592186576411 false] [17592186526090 1071 "If $y=\\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}^{2}-1)+\\operatorname{arsech}⁡({x}^{2}-1),$ calculate $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}.$\n\n$\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{2x}{{x}^{2}-1}[1-$\n{{field-1}} $]$" 13194139539448 17592186576411 true] [17592186526091 1071 "$$\n\n$\\int \\frac{2\\sqrt{2}}{|x|\\sqrt{2{x}^{2}+2}}\\,\\text{d}x=$" 13194139539448 17592186576411 false] [17592186526091 1071 "$$\n\\int \\frac{2\\sqrt{2}}{|x|\\sqrt{2{x}^{2}+2}}\\,\\text{d}x=\n$$" 13194139539448 17592186576411 true] [17592186526091 1074 "$$\n\nThe formula for the derivative of the inverse hyperbolic cosecant function is\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\operatorname{arcsch}⁡x)=-\\frac{1}{|x|\\sqrt{1+{x}^{2}}}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{2\\sqrt{2}}{|x|\\sqrt{2{x}^{2}+2}}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int \\frac{2\\sqrt{2}}{|x|\\sqrt{2({x}^{2}+1)}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-\\frac{2\\sqrt{2}}{\\sqrt{2}}\\int -\\frac{1}{|x|\\sqrt{1+{x}^{2}}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-2\\operatorname{arcsch}⁡x+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139539448 17592186576411 false] [17592186526091 1074 "The formula for the derivative of the inverse hyperbolic cosecant function is\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\operatorname{arcsch}⁡x)=-\\frac{1}{|x|\\sqrt{1+{x}^{2}}}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{2\\sqrt{2}}{|x|\\sqrt{2{x}^{2}+2}}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int \\frac{2\\sqrt{2}}{|x|\\sqrt{2({x}^{2}+1)}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-\\frac{2\\sqrt{2}}{\\sqrt{2}}\\int -\\frac{1}{|x|\\sqrt{1+{x}^{2}}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-2\\operatorname{arcsch}⁡x+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139539448 17592186576411 true] [17592186526103 1071 "$$\n\n$\\int \\frac{3}{4|x|\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+1}}\\,\\text{d}x=$" 13194139539448 17592186576411 false] [17592186526103 1071 "$$\n\\int \\frac{3}{4|x|\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+1}}\\,\\text{d}x=\n$$" 13194139539448 17592186576411 true] [17592186526103 1074 "$$\n\nThe formula for the derivative of the inverse hyperbolic cosecant function is\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\operatorname{arcsch}⁡x)=-\\frac{1}{|x|\\sqrt{1+{x}^{2}}}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{3}{4|x|\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+1}}\\,\\text{d}x=-\\frac{3}{4}\\int -\\frac{1}{|x|\\sqrt{1+{x}^{2}}}\\,\\text{d}x=-\\frac{3}{4}\\operatorname{arcsch}⁡x+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139539448 17592186576411 false] [17592186526103 1074 "The formula for the derivative of the inverse hyperbolic cosecant function is\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\operatorname{arcsch}⁡x)=-\\frac{1}{|x|\\sqrt{1+{x}^{2}}}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{3}{4|x|\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+1}}\\,\\text{d}x=-\\frac{3}{4}\\int -\\frac{1}{|x|\\sqrt{1+{x}^{2}}}\\,\\text{d}x=-\\frac{3}{4}\\operatorname{arcsch}⁡x+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139539448 17592186576411 true] [17592186526105 1074 "$$\nThe formula for the derivative of the inverse hyperbolic secant function is\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\operatorname{arsech}⁡x)=-\\frac{1}{x\\sqrt{1-{x}^{2}}}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int ({e}^{x/4}+\\frac{2}{x\\sqrt{1-{x}^{2}}})\\text{d}x & =\\int {e}^{x/4}\\,\\text{d}x+\\int \\frac{2}{x\\sqrt{1-{x}^{2}}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int {e}^{x/4}-2\\int -\\frac{1}{x\\sqrt{1-{x}^{2}}}\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =4{e}^{x/4}-2\\operatorname{arsech}⁡x+C \\\\  & =2(2{e}^{x/4}-\\operatorname{arsech}⁡x)+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139539448 17592186576411 false] [17592186526105 1074 "The formula for the derivative of the inverse hyperbolic secant function is\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\operatorname{arsech}⁡x)=-\\frac{1}{x\\sqrt{1-{x}^{2}}}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int ({e}^{x/4}+\\frac{2}{x\\sqrt{1-{x}^{2}}})\\text{d}x & =\\int {e}^{x/4}\\,\\text{d}x+\\int \\frac{2}{x\\sqrt{1-{x}^{2}}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int {e}^{x/4}-2\\int -\\frac{1}{x\\sqrt{1-{x}^{2}}}\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =4{e}^{x/4}-2\\operatorname{arsech}⁡x+C \\\\  & =2(2{e}^{x/4}-\\operatorname{arsech}⁡x)+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139539448 17592186576411 true] [17592186527137 1071 "Anna makes two cakes. The first cake weighs $1,200\\,\\text{g},$ while the second cake weighs $140%$ of the weight of the first. What is the weight of the second cake?" 13194139539448 17592186576411 false] [17592186527137 1071 "Anna makes two cakes. The first cake weighs $1,200\\,\\text{g},$ while the second cake weighs $140\\%$ of the weight of the first. What is the weight of the second cake?" 13194139539448 17592186576411 true] [17592186527137 1074 "To solve this problem, we can use the formula:\n\n$$\n\\text{part}=\\text{percentage}\\times \\text{whole}\n$$\n\nIn our case, the whole is the weight of the first cake, which is $1,200\\,\\text{g}.$ The percentage is $140%,$ and the part is the weight of the second cake.\n\n**Method 1**\n\nFirst, we convert the percentage to a decimal:\n\n$$\n140%=140÷100=1.4\n$$\n\nApplying our formula, we have:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{part} & =\\text{percentage}\\times \\text{whole} \\\\  & =140%\\times 1,200 \\\\  & =1.4\\times 1,200 \\\\  & =1,680\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $140%$ of $1,200$ is $1,680.$ So, the weight of the second cake is $1,680\\,\\text{g}.$\n\n**Method 2**\n\nFirst, we convert the percentage to a fraction:\n\n$$\n140%=\\frac{140}{100}=\\frac{140÷20}{100÷20}=\\frac{7}{5}\n$$\n\nApplying our formula, we have:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{part} & =\\text{percentage}\\times \\text{whole} \\\\  & =140%\\times 1,200 \\\\  & =\\frac{7}{5}\\times 1,200 \\\\  & =7\\times \\frac{1,200}{5} \\\\  & =7\\times 240 \\\\  & =1,680\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $140%$ of $1,200$ is $1,680.$ So, the weight of the second cake is $1,680\\,\\text{g}.$" 13194139539448 17592186576411 false] [17592186527137 1074 "To solve this problem, we can use the formula:\n\n$$\n\\text{part}=\\text{percentage}\\times \\text{whole}\n$$\n\nIn our case, the whole is the weight of the first cake, which is $1,200\\,\\text{g}.$ The percentage is $140\\%,$ and the part is the weight of the second cake.\n\n**Method 1**\n\nFirst, we convert the percentage to a decimal:\n\n$$\n140\\%=140÷100=1.4\n$$\n\nApplying our formula, we have:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{part} & =\\text{percentage}\\times \\text{whole} \\\\  & =140\\%\\times 1,200 \\\\  & =1.4\\times 1,200 \\\\  & =1,680\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $140\\%$ of $1,200$ is $1,680.$ So, the weight of the second cake is $1,680\\,\\text{g}.$\n\n**Method 2**\n\nFirst, we convert the percentage to a fraction:\n\n$$\n140\\%=\\frac{140}{100}=\\frac{140÷20}{100÷20}=\\frac{7}{5}\n$$\n\nApplying our formula, we have:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{part} & =\\text{percentage}\\times \\text{whole} \\\\  & =140\\%\\times 1,200 \\\\  & =\\frac{7}{5}\\times 1,200 \\\\  & =7\\times \\frac{1,200}{5} \\\\  & =7\\times 240 \\\\  & =1,680\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $140\\%$ of $1,200$ is $1,680.$ So, the weight of the second cake is $1,680\\,\\text{g}.$" 13194139539448 17592186576411 true] [17592186531578 1071 "Consider the following inhomogeneous system of linear differential equations:\n\n$$\n{x}^{′}(t)=[\\begin{aligned}0 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{aligned}]x(t)+[\\begin{aligned}2{t}^{2}+t+3 \\\\ -{t}^{2}+2t\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nThe complementary solution to this system is given by\n\n$$\n{x}_{c}(t)={c}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡t \\\\ \\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\end{aligned}]+{c}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}-\\operatorname{sin}⁡t \\\\ \\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\end{aligned}],\\,{c}_{1},{c}_{2}\\in R.\n$$\n\nThen, the general solution of the system is\n\n<table align=\"l\" cellpadding=\"0\" rules=\"all\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"40px\" rowspan=\"2\">\n    $x(t)={x}_{c}(t)+\\,\\,$\n  </td>\n<td height=\"30px\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\">$1$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"40px\" rowspan=\"2\">\n    $\\,\\,{t}^{2}+\\,\\,$\n  </td>\n<td height=\"30px\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\">\n    $2$\n  </td>\n<td align=\"center\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"40px\" rowspan=\"2\">\n    $\\,\\,t+\\,\\,$\n  </td>\n<td height=\"30px\" width=\"5