ext{otherwise}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, provided that $N≫n,$ the random variables ${X}_{i}$ can be considered independent and identically distributed. Under this assumption, we have\n\n$$\n{X}_{i}∼\\text{Bernoulli}(p)\\,1\\le i\\le n\n$$\n\nwhere $p$ is the proportion of the population that has the characteristic.\n\nTherefore, the random variable $X,$ defined as \n\n$$\nX={\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}{X}_{i}\n$$\n\ncan be approximated as a binomial random variable $X≈B(n,p),$ where\n\n$$\n\\text{E}[X]=np,\\,\\text{Var}[X]=np(1-p).\n$$\n\nIn our case, we're told that the population size is significantly larger than the sample size. Moreover, we have \n\n$$\np=5\\%=0.05,\\,n=120.\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\nX≈B(120,0.05)\n$$\n\nand we have the following results for the mean and variance:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{E}[X] & =np \\\\  & =120\\cdot 0.05 \\\\  & =6 \\\\ \\text{Var}[X] & =np(1-p) \\\\  & =120\\cdot 0.05\\cdot (1-0.05) \\\\  & =5.7\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139539448 17592186576411 true] [17592186555845 1071 "Suppose that $38%$ of a city's adult population like romance movies. A random sample of $n=30$ adults is taken from the population and asked about their favorite movie genre.\n\nWhat is the mean and variance of $\\widehat{\\,p},$ the proportion of people in the sample who like romance movies? Round your answers to $3$ decimal places where appropriate.\n\n*Hint: You may assume that the population size is significantly larger than the sample size.*" 13194139539448 17592186576411 false] [17592186555845 1071 "Suppose that $38\\%$ of a city's adult population like romance movies. A random sample of $n=30$ adults is taken from the population and asked about their favorite movie genre.\n\nWhat is the mean and variance of $\\widehat{\\,p},$ the proportion of people in the sample who like romance movies? Round your answers to $3$ decimal places where appropriate.\n\n*Hint: You may assume that the population size is significantly larger than the sample size.*" 13194139539448 17592186576411 true] [17592186555868 1071 "Rose's initial salary was $$10\\,000$, and her salary increased by $12%$ per year. To the nearest $$10$, what was Rose's salary $3$ years later?" 13194139539448 17592186576411 false] [17592186555868 1071 "Rose's initial salary was $\\$10\\,000$, and her salary increased by $12\\%$ per year. To the nearest $\\$10$, what was Rose's salary $3$ years later?" 13194139539448 17592186576411 true] [17592186555868 1074 "Rose received $$10\\,000$ initially, and this amount increased by $12%$ each year.\n\n$12%$ as a decimal is $0.12.$ Therefore, an increase of $12%$ corresponds to multiplication by a factor of\n\n$$\n1+0.12=1.12.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have:\n\n- After $1$ year, Rose received $10\\,000\\cdot (1.12)$ dollars.\n\n- After $2$ years, Rose received $10\\,000\\cdot (1.12)^{2}$ dollars.\n\n- After $3$ years, Rose received $10\\,000\\cdot (1.12)^{3}$ dollars.\n\nEvaluating the expression for the amount of money received after $3$ years, we get\n\n$$\n10\\,000\\cdot (1.12)^{3}≈14\\,050.\n$$\n\nAfter $3$ years, Rose received approximately $14\\,050$ dollars." 13194139539448 17592186576411 false] [17592186555868 1074 "Rose received $\\$10\\,000$ initially, and this amount increased by $12\\%$ each year.\n\n$12\\%$ as a decimal is $0.12.$ Therefore, an increase of $12\\%$ corresponds to multiplication by a factor of\n\n$$\n1+0.12=1.12.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have:\n\n- After $1$ year, Rose received $10\\,000\\cdot (1.12)$ dollars.\n\n- After $2$ years, Rose received $10\\,000\\cdot (1.12)^{2}$ dollars.\n\n- After $3$ years, Rose received $10\\,000\\cdot (1.12)^{3}$ dollars.\n\nEvaluating the expression for the amount of money received after $3$ years, we get\n\n$$\n10\\,000\\cdot (1.12)^{3}≈14\\,050.\n$$\n\nAfter $3$ years, Rose received approximately $14\\,050$ dollars." 13194139539448 17592186576411 true] [17592186558483 1074 "The given expression is an exponential growth expression of the form $y(t)=a\\cdot {b}^{t}$, where:\n\n- $a=1\\,000$ represents the initial population of ants\n\n- $b=1.5$ is the growth factor\n\n- $t=4$ is the time in months since the start of the observations\n\nFor the factor $(1.5)^{4},$ the growth rate $(1.5)$ means that the population grows by $50%$ per month, and the exponent $(4)$ gives the number of months. \n\nTherefore, the ant population grew by a factor of $(1.5)^{4}$ over the first $4$ months." 13194139539448 17592186576411 false] [17592186558483 1074 "The given expression is an exponential growth expression of the form $y(t)=a\\cdot {b}^{t}$, where:\n\n- $a=1\\,000$ represents the initial population of ants\n\n- $b=1.5$ is the growth factor\n\n- $t=4$ is the time in months since the start of the observations\n\nFor the factor $(1.5)^{4},$ the growth rate $(1.5)$ means that the population grows by $50\\%$ per month, and the exponent $(4)$ gives the number of months. \n\nTherefore, the ant population grew by a factor of $(1.5)^{4}$ over the first $4$ months." 13194139539448 17592186576411 true] [17592186558494 1071 "Determine which of the following is the graph of $x=\\frac{2\\sqrt{y}+8}{{y}^{3/2}}\\,$ by completing the following table:\n\n| **$y$** | $1$ | $4$ | $9$ | $16$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $x$ |  |  |  |  |" 13194139539448 17592186576411 true] [17592186558494 1071 "Determine which of the following is the graph of $x=\\frac{2\\sqrt{y}+8}{{y}^{3/2}}\\,$ by completing the following table:\n\n| **$y$** | $1$ | $4$ | $9$ | $16$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $x$ | $$ | $$ | $$ | $$ |" 13194139539448 17592186576411 false] [17592186558505 1071 "Determine which of the following is the graph of $x=(2y+1)^{2}-6\\,$ by completing the following table:\n\n| **$y$** | $-\\frac{1}{2}$ | $0$ | $1$ | $\\frac{3}{2}$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $x$ |  |  |  |  |" 13194139539448 17592186576411 true] [17592186558505 1071 "Determine which of the following is the graph of $x=(2y+1)^{2}-6\\,$ by completing the following table:\n\n| **$y$**