mes \\frac{5}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{32}{2}\\times 5 \\\\  & =16\\times 5 \\\\  & =80\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139539448 17592186576411 true] [17592186566251 1071 "Nathan invested $\\$5\\,600$ into a company which then went on to lose $7%$ of its value every year. Which expression gives the value of Nathan's investment after $3$ years?" 13194139539448 17592186576411 false] [17592186566251 1071 "Nathan invested $\\$5\\,600$ into a company which then went on to lose $7\\%$ of its value every year. Which expression gives the value of Nathan's investment after $3$ years?" 13194139539448 17592186576411 true] [17592186566251 1074 "The number $7%$ (expressed as a decimal) is equal to $0.07.$ Therefore, a decrease of $7%$ corresponds to multiplication by a factor of:\n\n$$\n1-0.07=0.93\n$$\n\nTherefore:\n\n- After $1$ year, the value of the investment was $5\\,600\\cdot (0.93)$ dollars.\n\n- After $2$ years, the value of the investment was $5\\,600\\cdot (0.93)^{2}$ dollars.\n\n- After $3$ years, the value of the investment was $5\\,600\\cdot (0.93)^{3}$ dollars." 13194139539448 17592186576411 false] [17592186566251 1074 "The number $7\\%$ (expressed as a decimal) is equal to $0.07.$ Therefore, a decrease of $7\\%$ corresponds to multiplication by a factor of:\n\n$$\n1-0.07=0.93\n$$\n\nTherefore:\n\n- After $1$ year, the value of the investment was $5\\,600\\cdot (0.93)$ dollars.\n\n- After $2$ years, the value of the investment was $5\\,600\\cdot (0.93)^{2}$ dollars.\n\n- After $3$ years, the value of the investment was $5\\,600\\cdot (0.93)^{3}$ dollars." 13194139539448 17592186576411 true] [17592186579527 1071 "At the start of a study, a hive had $2\\,000$ bees. The study shows that the number of bees in the hive is expected to increase by $20%$ every month. What equation should be solved to determine the time that it will take for there to be $5\\,000$ bees in the hive?" 13194139539448 17592186576411 false] [17592186579527 1071 "At the start of a study, a hive had $2\\,000$ 